# ---- Defensely: added when this repo was split out ----
# Function app settings hold real credentials. Commit the .sample file instead.
local.settings.json
**/local.settings.json
!**/local.settings.sample.json
*.csproj.user
# ---- Config that MUST be committed ----
# The blanket *.json rule above would otherwise exclude application config.
# In the old repo these survived only because they were already tracked.
!**/appsettings.json
!**/appsettings.*.json
!**/host.json
!**/Properties/launchSettings.json
!.config/dotnet-tools.json
# Sample config carries no secrets and is the only documentation of some keys.
!**/*.sample.json
# Postman collections are test assets, not config.
!**/*.postman_collection.json

# ...but never the real function secrets
local.settings.json
**/local.settings.json
!**/local.settings.sample.json
# ---- Never commit key material ----
*.p12
*.pfx
*.pem
*.key
# Generated from docs/html by scripts/md2html.ps1 + headless Edge. Regenerable, so not tracked.
docs/pdf/

# ---- The vendored DLP.RegexFilter pattern set ----
# There is a blanket `*.json` higher up this file, and it swallows patterns.json —
# which IS the scanner. Without that file the engine loads no patterns, matches
# nothing, and reports every document clean. Nothing errors; a scan just comes back
# empty. Negated explicitly here, because the failure is invisible.
!DLP.RegexFilter/patterns.json
# filetypes.json arrived with the 22.10 hand-over and the same `*.json` rule swallows it.
# Milder than patterns.json - FileTypeCatalogue reads it to label a result, and routing is
# driven by the extension sets in DlpScanner, so losing it costs display names rather than
# coverage. Tracked anyway: a file the library ships should not be missing in CI only.
!DLP.RegexFilter/filetypes.json
